From 792a1aa90033afdda1206a3892ced6c165d5ddb6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 00:38:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 17/23] x24: keep batch 1024, cap in-flight rollouts at 256

At max_inflight_rollouts=1024 the tunnel layer saturated: all 24 tunnels
wedged at once, and once the watchdog was fixed it settled into an
equilibrium rebuilding 10-14 per 45s cycle while they re-wedged just as fast.
Engines fell to 1-6 concurrent because the churn killed in-flight requests.

Batch size and in-flight concurrency are separable. 1024 batch with 16-rollout
groups is what gives the low-variance gradient; concurrency only decides how
fast it is gathered. 256 in flight is the level that ran clean for 36 steps in
x22, so collection is ~4x longer but the tunnels hold.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017wiESxhziDrnsLnG9aizTd
